cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "gene-edit-check: a computational-biology toolkit for cell-state-selective CRISPR base edits"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mendiratta
    given-names: Arav
repository-code: "https://github.com/aravmendiratta/gene-edit-check"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
keywords:
  - AlphaGenome
  - CRISPR base editing
  - single-cell genomics
  - T-cell exhaustion
  - regulatory genomics
abstract: >-
  A verifier-guided search for cell-state-selective CRISPR base edits that uses Google DeepMind's
  AlphaGenome 2 as the judge. Applied to PDCD1 (PD-1) silencing in exhausted tumour-infiltrating
  CD8 T cells from colorectal cancer (Pelka et al., Cell 2021), no candidate edit passes every safety check;
  CpG methylation is the binding constraint. Edit efficacy and predicted CpG methylation shift are positively
  associated (Spearman rho about +0.5 to +0.6 across seeds, cohorts and six checkpoint loci), a moderate
  association whose specificity to methylation is not established. Model predictions only; no wet-lab validation.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Pelka
        given-names: Karin
    title: "Spatially organized multicellular immune hubs in human colorectal cancer"
    journal: Cell
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1016/j.cell.2021.08.003
